0..77 Comment "// An atom named inside the abstraction that binds it (Fernández and Gabbay,"
78..157 Comment "// _Nominal rewriting_, I&C 2007, § 2; Pitts, _Nominal Sets_, CUP 2013, § 4)."
158..237 Comment "// Inside `bind a . t` the name `a` is the atom `a`, and outside it a variable."
238..313 Comment "// Admission re-mints an atom with the abstraction that binds it, so a rule"
314..391 Comment "// naming the channel its restriction abstracts is one rule whatever the atom"
392..466 Comment "// is called: matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s replay read an"
467..543 Comment "// occurrence by the number of abstractions between it and its binder. Where"
544..620 Comment "// a port takes an atom, a term can name one, and a rule stating a freshness"
621..699 Comment "// condition, or moving a variable across an abstraction, fires only where its"
700..779 Comment "// instance names no atom it may not, counting the atoms a moved instance names"
780..853 Comment "// to their abstractions\' new places. Such a rule overlapping another, or"
854..932 Comment "// matching a variable both under an abstraction and beside it, is not decided"
933..991 Comment "// yet (#1934): `pathological/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr`."
993..1069 Comment "/// A send on a restricted channel, which no process outside the restriction"
1070..1147 Comment "/// can receive: the process never moves, so it is the inert one. The checker"
1148..1224 Comment "/// orients the law and the kernel replays the verdict; a restriction naming"
1225..1284 Comment "/// its channel `b` normalizes by the law written over `a`."
1285..1287 Other "@["
1288..1298 Other "normalizes"
1298..1299 Other "("
1299..1300 StringLit "\""
1300..1331 StringLit "nu(bind b . out(b, nil)) ~> nil"
1331..1332 StringLit "\""
